IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lta-common`

-- Taxation Administration Act 1996 (SA) -- interest, penalty tax, objections and appeals, as they apply to land tax.
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE: the rules are in the Act's own actors and terms ("the taxpayer", "the objector", "the Minister",
-- "the Commissioner"). The individual's questions are in lta-seat.l4.
--
-- SOURCE. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, through the Open Australian Legal Corpus
-- (CC BY 4.0; see lta-common.l4 and SOURCE-LICENSE.md). The deposited text is the version of 2019-10-03 (corpus
-- version_id south_australian_legislation:2019-10-03/1996.80.un, scraped 2024-09-13), at
-- ../../../taxation-administration-act-1996/registers/source-bundle/taxation-administration-act-1996.txt. It is not the
-- official text. The Current Titles list of 22 September 2026 lists the Act at 4.12.2025, so at least one later version
-- is not reflected here.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: Part 5 Division 1: s 25 (interest on a tax default, daily, from the end of the last day for
-- payment), s 26 (market rate plus 8% a year; the market rate is an INPUT), s 27 (nil under $20); Part 5 Division 2:
-- s 30 (penalty tax; none if the Commissioner is satisfied the default was neither deliberate nor careless), s 31 (75% or
-- 25%, less 80% or 20% for a sufficient disclosure, plus up to 20% for obstructive conduct), s 32 (nil under $20), s 33
-- (pay within the period in the assessment; regulative); Part 10: s 84 (objection to a reassessment), s 86 (60 days),
-- s 87 (late objection, at most 12 months), s 91 (no suspension of recovery), s 92 (right of appeal), s 93 (50% of the
-- tax paid first), s 94 (60 days; or at any time on 14 days' notice when the Minister has not decided within 90 days),
-- s 95 (late appeal, at most 12 months); ss 92-95 together for an appeal on a given day; Part 10 as a regulative rule.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: assessment and reassessment machinery (Part 3) except as named; refunds (Part 4); special tax return
-- arrangements (Part 6); tax avoidance schemes (Part 6A); collection (Part 7); records and offences (Part 8);
-- investigation and secrecy (Part 9); interest on refunds (ss 90, 99); remission of interest and penalty tax (ss 29, 34:
-- the Commissioner's discretion, unbounded); s 102 (rounding down to a dollar: the Commissioner "may").
--
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Taxation Administration Act 1996 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Part 5 Division 1 -- interest on a tax default (ss 25-27)`

-- s 3(1): "tax default means failure by a taxpayer to pay, in accordance with a taxation law, the whole or part of tax that
-- the taxpayer is liable to pay".
-- s 25(1): "If a tax default occurs, the taxpayer is liable to pay interest on the amount of tax unpaid calculated on a
-- daily basis from the end of the last day for payment until the day it is paid at the interest rate from time to time
-- applying under this Division." (2): interest is payable on unpaid penalty tax "but is not payable in respect of any
-- failure to pay interest".
-- s 26(1): the rate is "the sum of -- (a) the market rate; and (b) 8 per cent per annum". (2): the market rate is "(a)
-- ... the average rate of the daily 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate prescribed by the Reserve Bank of Australia for the
-- month of May preceding the financial year (rounding up 0.005 to 2 decimal places); or (b) the rate specified from time
-- to time by order of the Minister published in the Gazette". Neither figure is deposited: the market rate is an INPUT.
-- s 27: "If the amount of interest payable for the time being in respect of a tax default would, apart from this section,
-- be less than $20, no interest is payable".
-- READING: "a daily basis" is the annual rate divided by 365 for each day; the Act does not say whether a leap year
-- counts 366. One rate is applied to the whole period (the rate "from time to time" changes each financial year; a period
-- crossing 30 June is not split here).
`the interest premium, percent a year` MEANS 8

GIVEN `the May average of the daily 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the market rate from the May average` MEANS
    `rounded to 2 decimal places, 0.005 up` `the May average of the daily 90-day Bank Accepted Bill Rate`

GIVEN `the market rate, percent a year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest rate, percent a year` MEANS
    `the market rate, percent a year` PLUS `the interest premium, percent a year`

GIVEN `the amount of tax unpaid` IS A NUMBER
      `the market rate, percent a year` IS A NUMBER
      `the last day for payment` IS A DATE
      `the day it is paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest on the tax default` MEANS
    IF `accrued` LESS THAN 20
    THEN 0
    ELSE `accrued`
    WHERE
        `days` MEANS `the greater of` 0 (`the days from` `the last day for payment` `to` `the day it is paid`)
        `annual interest` MEANS
            (`the amount of tax unpaid` TIMES (`the interest rate, percent a year` `the market rate, percent a year`)) DIVIDED BY 100
        `accrued` MEANS (`annual interest` TIMES `days`) DIVIDED BY 365

§§ `Part 5 Division 2 -- penalty tax (ss 30-33)`

-- s 30(1): "If a tax default occurs, the taxpayer is liable to pay penalty tax in addition to the amount of the tax
-- unpaid." (2): "Penalty tax is not payable in respect of a tax default if the Commissioner is satisfied that the tax
-- default was not a deliberate tax default and did not result, wholly or partly, from any failure by the taxpayer, or a
-- person acting on the taxpayer's behalf, to take reasonable care to comply with the requirements of a taxation law."
-- (4): none for a failure to pay interest or earlier penalty tax.
-- s 31(1): "(a) in the case of a deliberate tax default -- 75 per cent of the amount of tax unpaid; or (b) in any other
-- case -- 25 per cent". (2): "(a) if the taxpayer made a sufficient disclosure of the tax default while not subject to a
-- tax audit -- the penalty tax is to be reduced by 80 per cent; (b) if the taxpayer made a sufficient disclosure ...
-- while subject to a tax audit -- ... reduced by 20 per cent; (c) if the taxpayer engaged in obstructive conduct while
-- subject to a tax audit -- the penalty tax may be increased by the Commissioner by 20 per cent."
-- s 32: "If the amount of penalty tax ... would, apart from this section, be less than $20, no penalty tax is payable".
-- s 3(1) "deliberate tax default" and s 31(3) "tax audit", "sufficient disclosure" and "obstructive conduct" are taken as
-- FACTS; the Commissioner's satisfaction (s 30(2)) and the increase (s 31(2)(c)) are the Commissioner's: the answer is
-- conditional on them. READING: "reduced by 80 per cent" is 80% of the penalty tax off; a disclosure while not subject
-- to an audit is taken first; the reduction and the increase, where both apply, are multiplied.
DECLARE `Penalty tax facts` HAS
    `the amount of tax unpaid`                                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the tax default was deliberate`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is satisfied the default was not deliberate and not from a lack of reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a sufficient disclosure was made while not subject to a tax audit`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a sufficient disclosure was made while subject to a tax audit`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner increases it for obstructive conduct during a tax audit`                   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax rate before adjustment, percent` MEANS
    IF `p`'s `the tax default was deliberate` THEN 75 ELSE 25

GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax adjustment, percent of the penalty tax` MEANS
    `the disclosure factor` TIMES `the obstruction factor` DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the disclosure factor` MEANS
            IF `p`'s `a sufficient disclosure was made while not subject to a tax audit`
            THEN 20
            ELSE IF `p`'s `a sufficient disclosure was made while subject to a tax audit`
                 THEN 80
                 ELSE 100
        `the obstruction factor` MEANS
            IF `p`'s `the Commissioner increases it for obstructive conduct during a tax audit` THEN 120 ELSE 100

GIVEN `p` IS A `Penalty tax facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty tax` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`p`'s `the tax default was deliberate`))
       AND `p`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied the default was not deliberate and not from a lack of reasonable care`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `adjusted` LESS THAN 20
         THEN 0
         ELSE `adjusted`
    WHERE
        `unadjusted` MEANS
            (`p`'s `the amount of tax unpaid` TIMES (`the penalty tax rate before adjustment, percent` `p`)) DIVIDED BY 100
        `adjusted` MEANS
            (`unadjusted` TIMES (`the penalty tax adjustment, percent of the penalty tax` `p`)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 33: "Penalty tax must be paid by a taxpayer within the period specified for that purpose in an assessment of the tax
-- liability of the taxpayer." The period is the assessment's: an INPUT. Clock: days from service of the assessment.
GIVEN `the days specified in the assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`TAA s 33 -- pay the penalty tax within the period specified in the assessment` MEANS
    PARTY `the taxpayer`
    MUST  `pay the penalty tax`
    WITHIN `the days specified in the assessment`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the taxpayer` BECAUSE "TAA s 33: penalty tax must be paid within the period specified in the assessment; interest then runs on it (s 25(2)), but no further penalty tax (s 30(4))"

§§ `Part 10 Division 1 -- objections (ss 82, 84, 86, 87, 91)`

-- s 82: "A person who is dissatisfied with -- (a) an assessment (other than a compromise assessment); or (b) a decision
-- under Part 4 concerning a refund ...; or (c) any other decision of the Commissioner under a taxation law that is not
-- declared to be a non-reviewable decision, may lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister." s 83: "The grounds
-- of an objection must be stated fully and in detail".
-- s 84: "In the case of an objection to a reassessment, the objection may only relate to tax liabilities specified in the
-- reassessment to the extent that they are additional to or greater than those under the previous assessment."
GIVEN `it is a reassessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount assessed before` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount assessed now` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount open to objection` MEANS
    IF `it is a reassessment`
    THEN `the greater of` 0 (`the amount assessed now` MINUS `the amount assessed before`)
    ELSE `the amount assessed now`

-- s 86: "An objection must be lodged with the Minister not later than 60 days after -- (a) in the case of an objection to
-- an assessment -- the date of service of the assessment on the taxpayer; or (b) in the case of an objection to some other
-- decision -- the date on which the taxpayer was notified of the decision."
`the days to object` MEANS 60

-- s 87(1): "The Minister has a discretion to permit a person to lodge an objection after the end of the 60-day period but
-- not to do so later than 12 months after" the same date. (2): the notice must state "fully and in detail" the reasons for
-- the delay. (3): a refusal is non-reviewable.
`the months within which the Minister may allow a late objection` MEANS 12

GIVEN `the date of service of the assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the Minister may allow a late objection` MEANS
    `years after` (`the months within which the Minister may allow a late objection` DIVIDED BY 12) `the date of service of the assessment`

-- s 91: "The fact that an objection is pending does not in the meantime affect the assessment or decision to which the
-- objection relates and tax may be recovered as if no objection were pending."
`an objection suspends recovery of the tax` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Part 10 Division 2 -- appeals (ss 92-95)`

-- s 92: "A person who has made an objection may appeal to the Supreme Court if -- (a) the person is dissatisfied with the
-- Minister's determination of the objection; or (b) 90 days (not including any period of suspension under section 88)
-- have passed since the objection was lodged with the Minister and the Minister has not determined the objection and
-- served notice of the determination on the person."
`the days the Minister has before an appeal may be made without a determination` MEANS 90

GIVEN `the Minister has determined the objection and served notice of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the outcome` IS AN `Objection outcome`
      `the days since the objection was lodged, not counting any suspension under s 88` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objector has a right of appeal under s 92` IF
    IF `the Minister has determined the objection and served notice of it`
    THEN CONSIDER `the outcome`
         WHEN `the objection is allowed in full` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE
    ELSE `the days since the objection was lodged, not counting any suspension under s 88`
             AT LEAST `the days the Minister has before an appeal may be made without a determination`

-- s 93(1): "A taxpayer cannot exercise a right of appeal unless the taxpayer has paid to the Commissioner 50% of the whole
-- of the tax (not including interest and penalty tax under Part 5) to which the appeal relates as assessed by the
-- Commissioner or by the Minister on the objection." (2): the Minister may permit it anyway; (3): a refusal is
-- non-reviewable.
`the percentage of the tax to be paid before an appeal` MEANS 50

GIVEN `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of that tax paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister permits the appeal without that payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 93 does not bar the appeal` IF
        `the amount of that tax paid` AT LEAST
            `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax` TIMES `the percentage of the tax to be paid before an appeal` DIVIDED BY 100
    OR  `the Minister permits the appeal without that payment`

-- s 94(1): "An appeal must be made by a person not later than 60 days after the date of service on the person of notice of
-- the Minister's determination of the person's objection." (2): if 90 days (not counting a suspension) have passed and the
-- Minister has not determined and served notice, "the person may appeal at any time provided that the Commissioner is
-- given not less than 14 days written notice of the person's intention to make the appeal".
-- s 95: "The Supreme Court has a discretion to allow a person to appeal after the end of the 60-day period but not to do
-- so later than 12 months after the date of service on the person of notice of the Minister's determination".
`the days to appeal` MEANS 60

`the days of notice to the Commissioner before an appeal on an undetermined objection` MEANS 14

`the months within which the Supreme Court may allow a late appeal` MEANS 12

GIVEN `the date of service of notice of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the Supreme Court may allow a late appeal` MEANS
    `years after` (`the months within which the Supreme Court may allow a late appeal` DIVIDED BY 12) `the date of service of notice of the determination`

-- Whether an appeal made on a given day may proceed: the right (s 92), the payment (s 93) and the time (ss 94, 95), all
-- three. The Supreme Court's leave under s 95 and the Minister's permission under s 93(2) are theirs: the answer is
-- conditional on them. On the determined road the appeal is in time from the day of service up to and including the
-- 60th day after it (s 94(1)), or, with the Court's leave, up to and including the same day 12 months after service
-- (s 95). On the undetermined road (s 94(2)) it is in time on or after the 14th day after the Commissioner was given
-- written notice. Clock: calendar days between the dates given.
DECLARE `Appeal facts` HAS
    `the Minister has determined the objection and served notice of it`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the outcome`                                                                     IS AN `Objection outcome`
    `the days since the objection was lodged, not counting any suspension under s 88` IS A NUMBER
    `the date of service of notice of the determination`                              IS A DATE
    `the Commissioner has been given written notice of the intention to appeal`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the Commissioner was given that notice`                                 IS A DATE
    `the date of the appeal`                                                          IS A DATE
    `the Supreme Court allows the appeal out of time`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax`                              IS A NUMBER
    `the amount of that tax paid`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister permits the appeal without that payment`                            IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS AN `Appeal facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is made in time under s 94 or s 95` IF
    IF `a`'s `the Minister has determined the objection and served notice of it`
    THEN     `days since service` AT LEAST 0
         AND (    `days since service` AT MOST `the days to appeal`
              OR  (    `a`'s `the Supreme Court allows the appeal out of time`
                   AND DATE_SERIAL (`a`'s `the date of the appeal`) AT MOST DATE_SERIAL (`the last day the Supreme Court may allow a late appeal` (`a`'s `the date of service of notice of the determination`))))
    ELSE     `a`'s `the Commissioner has been given written notice of the intention to appeal`
         AND `the days from` (`a`'s `the date the Commissioner was given that notice`) `to` (`a`'s `the date of the appeal`) AT LEAST `the days of notice to the Commissioner before an appeal on an undetermined objection`
    WHERE
        `days since service` MEANS `the days from` (`a`'s `the date of service of notice of the determination`) `to` (`a`'s `the date of the appeal`)

GIVEN `a` IS AN `Appeal facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objector may appeal to the Supreme Court on that day` IF
        `the objector has a right of appeal under s 92` (`a`'s `the Minister has determined the objection and served notice of it`) (`a`'s `the outcome`) (`a`'s `the days since the objection was lodged, not counting any suspension under s 88`)
    AND `s 93 does not bar the appeal` (`a`'s `the tax assessed, without interest and penalty tax`) (`a`'s `the amount of that tax paid`) (`a`'s `the Minister permits the appeal without that payment`)
    AND `the appeal is made in time under s 94 or s 95` `a`

-- The regulative rule. Clock: days, from the date of service of the assessment (s 86(a)). Objecting and appealing are
-- the person's choice, so not doing them is no breach (DO ... LEST FULFILLED). s 89(1): the Minister "must give written
-- notice to the objector of the determination of the objection" with reasons (s 89(2)); no period is stated, but after
-- 90 days (plus any s 88 suspension) without it, s 92(b) and s 94(2) open an appeal at any time on notice. That is the
-- LEST branch of the Minister's step: the Minister's delay is not a breach, it opens the other road.
-- The 14-day notice in s 94(2) is a lower bound on the day of the appeal, which a WITHIN cannot state; the earliest day
-- is given as a date in the seat layer.
GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN `Objection outcome`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`the appeal after the Minister's determination` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `the objection is allowed in full` THEN FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE
        PARTY `the objector`
        DO    `appeal to the Supreme Court`
        WITHIN `the days to appeal`
        LEST  FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`the appeal on an objection the Minister has not determined` MEANS
    PARTY `the objector`
    MAY   `give the Commissioner written notice of the intention to appeal`
    HENCE (PARTY `the objector`
           MAY   `appeal to the Supreme Court`)

GIVEN `the days of suspension under s 88` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Land tax party` `Land tax act`
`TAA Part 10 -- object within 60 days, then appeal within 60 days of the determination` MEANS
    PARTY `the objector`
    DO    `lodge a written notice of objection with the Minister, stating the grounds fully and in detail`
    WITHIN `the days to object`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Minister`
           DO    `give written notice of the determination of the objection, with reasons` `outcome`
           WITHIN `the days the Minister has before an appeal may be made without a determination` PLUS `the days of suspension under s 88`
           HENCE `the appeal after the Minister's determination` `outcome`
           LEST  `the appeal on an objection the Minister has not determined`)
    LEST  FULFILLED
